{
  "description": "The answer key for describer quality on Data/Images/Test/All: every object the shipped pipeline finds, numbered in its order in the frame, with what it is. Read and scored by Vision/Utilities/Evaluation.py; run with Example/Vision/evaluate_describer.py. Confirmed by the owner, 2026-09-29.",
  "rules": {
    "type": "Correct when the text names the part type or a synonym (the class's \"correct\" patterns, plurals included), and nothing contradicts it. A naming claim is the noun phrase after a naming cue (\"is a\", \"appears to be a\", \"possibly a\", \"suggesting it is a\", \"resembles a\" ...; \"naming_cues\"), up to the next clause (\"naming_ends\"), in any sentence. Wrong when a naming claim names a wrong type (the class's \"wrong\" patterns) or another part type (\"type_nouns\") and the text never names the right one; not decidable for an \"undecidable\" pattern in a claim; otherwise not stated (a generic \"component\", \"object\" or \"part\"). Conflicting names are a hedge, not stated, as \"plastic or painted metal\" is for material: the right type named and another part type claimed (\"washer or cap\", \"washer or ring\", or a wrong name in a later sentence). Synonyms are no conflict (\"bolt or screw\"). A feature is not a claim (\"the outer white ring\", \"the metal ring\": no naming cue); a ring that is a feature inside a claim (\"outer ring\", \"ring design\") is not one either.",
    "material": "The text's materials, sorted into metal and plastic by \"materials\", and other materials by \"other_materials\" (felt, fabric, ceramic, composite ...). Hedges score as the type's do: the right material named beside any other material (\"plastic or painted metal\", \"plastic or ceramic\") is not stated. The right material alone is correct. A wrong material, alone or beside another (\"metallic or composite\" on a plastic part), is wrong, and so is another material named alone (\"felt or fabric\"), as every part in the key is metal or plastic. None: not stated.",
    "colour": "Judged against the crop the describer receives, which is contrast-stretched: correct when the text names one of the object's colour terms, otherwise not stated. A wrong colour is not scored: the text also names the table's green seen through holes, which a word match cannot tell from the part's colour.",
    "totals": "Every object counts in the totals (the owner, 2026-09-29); a \"note\" records what is special about one.",
    "markings": "Markings and damage are recorded, not scored."
  },
